2DA V1.0
*
# ethren (M3.1): the occupations' weapons and trade goods (dccoccup.2da's WEAPON and GOOD), for the funnel's
# rolling screen. ITEM is the item a new peasant gets (* none yet: the rolling screen logs it and the OCCU
# record keeps an empty name); a game or test game ships its own copy with its items. NAME is what the card
# shows (_ for spaces); AS the weapon whose statistics a tool uses ("pitchfork (as spear)"); AMMO the row of
# the 1d6 ammunition a missile weapon comes with (sling stones, darts); CP the copper a money good is worth
# (it goes into the party's purse, counted in cp). FARMER_1-8 name the farmer's crop, CART_1-6 the pushcart's
# contents, ANIMAL_1-6 a duplicate farmer's or herder's animal (funnel.md, Table 1-3's footnotes).
            ITEM      NAME                    AS         AMMO    CP
